WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.376 --> 00:00:03.128
What if social media
could save lives?

00:00:06.758 --> 00:00:08.133
Right now, there are

00:00:08.176 --> 00:00:10.178
literally millions
of people

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:11.875
struggling with
undiagnosed

00:00:11.918 --> 00:00:13.138
medical conditions.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:16.225
I’m Breteni,

00:00:16.266 --> 00:00:17.268
Kamiyah’s mom.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:18.770
She’s 6 years old.

00:00:19.103 --> 00:00:24.650
She’s paralyzed anywhere
from 3 to 20 seconds,

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:26.110
over 300 times a day.

00:00:26.235 --> 00:00:28.405
I was in the Gulf War.

00:00:28.446 --> 00:00:30.576
I served 8 years,
and now

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:32.491
I’m losing my memory.

00:00:32.825 --> 00:00:34.701
Every time the
deja-vu happens

00:00:34.743 --> 00:00:36.578
I feel my eyes roll
in the back of my head,

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:37.830
and then I flatline.

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:40.333
Sadie has this
incurable disease,

00:00:40.375 --> 00:00:42.168
that the only thing
you can do is, you know,

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:43.670
remove half
of her brain.

00:00:43.711 --> 00:00:44.631
How could that be

00:00:44.675 --> 00:00:46.421
the only thing you
do to a kid?

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:48.633
My body is going
through something.

00:00:48.966 --> 00:00:51.010
The doctors are like,
“We can’t help you.”

00:00:51.218 --> 00:00:53.261
I want to know if
somebody else has this.

00:00:53.805 --> 00:00:55.098
They need
something different.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.933
The kind of thinking
that happens usually

00:00:57.975 --> 00:00:59.351
outside the hospital.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:01.928
I’m Dr. Lisa Sanders

00:01:01.971 --> 00:01:04.023
and I’m a physician
at Yale.

00:01:04.315 --> 00:01:05.691
For the past 15 years,

00:01:05.733 --> 00:01:06.755
I’ve written
a column for

00:01:06.798 --> 00:01:07.943
the New York Times
magazine

00:01:07.985 --> 00:01:09.073
about patients who

00:01:09.116 --> 00:01:10.696
have mysterious
symptoms.

00:01:10.738 --> 00:01:13.156
But, I always wanted
to go the next step.

00:01:13.783 --> 00:01:15.496
Using the internet,
we have

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:16.995
the ability to harness

00:01:17.036 --> 00:01:18.238
all of the intelligence

00:01:18.281 --> 00:01:19.746
of people around
the planet

00:01:19.788 --> 00:01:21.123
to get some answers.

00:01:22.333 --> 00:01:25.628
I was thrilled to see
that many responses.

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:26.838
It’s what we hoped for.

00:01:28.465 --> 00:01:30.258
Never, ever,
ever give up.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.780
There is somebody
out there

00:01:31.823 --> 00:01:32.801
that understands.

00:01:32.843 --> 00:01:33.938
The symptoms
align perfectly

00:01:33.981 --> 00:01:35.513
with the things that
I’ve experienced.

00:01:36.973 --> 00:01:39.183
There’s another mom
out there like me

00:01:39.225 --> 00:01:41.143
that was looking
for an answer.

00:01:41.518 --> 00:01:43.270
We’re not the only ones.

00:01:44.521 --> 00:01:46.523
You’ve got to keep
a positive attitude.

00:01:47.775 --> 00:01:48.943
It’s good news.

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:51.278
We can create
a movement.

00:01:51.821 --> 00:01:52.613
There’s hope.

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:57.160
1, 2...

00:01:59.411 --> 00:02:00.538
Are you trying
to kick me?

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:01.788
No!

00:02:01.831 --> 00:02:03.583
I did not do it
on purpose.

00:02:03.625 --> 00:02:04.500
I know.

